Package: jvs-archive-keyring
Version: 1.0.0
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Jake Van Slyke <pkgs@jvs.sh>
Description: GnuPG archive key and apt source for the jvs.sh repository
 Ships the public key apt uses to verify packages from pkgs.jvs.sh, along
 with the sources entry pointing at it.
 .
 Shipping these as a package rather than writing them from a setup script is
 what makes key rotation possible: a new signing key reaches installed
 machines through apt upgrade, like any other update. Removing this package
 removes the repository configuration.
